From cf10af89cce392993b6514d252fa21515c9e2a41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xbox360 Blades <xbox360-blades@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 18:07:02 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 31/51] Auto Sign-In at power-on; the Guide shows the signed-in
 gamertag

Power-on (new cvar power_on, set by the launcher for its first dashboard):
nobody signed in from before, and the Auto Sign-In profile
(XCONFIG_USER_DEFAULT_PROFILE) signs into slot 0 when retail flag 0x40 is
set and it is not recovering, as xam's power-on sign-in request does (818C1040
-> 818EBE88, flags 0xA44; 0x200 handled at 818EA78C). Title switches keep
who is signed in. Deleting that profile turns Auto Sign-In off (818EA210).

The Guide draws hudbkgnd's GamerTag down the blade: the gamertag of the
profile on the Guide's controller (xam 818D4218), placed by its keyframes
and the captured transform (gamertag.txt from make_guide_assets.py).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
